From: N10 Mainline Linux Project
Subject: drm/panel: panel-simple: adjust vtotal for scan-out alignment

The Hanvon N10 panel scans the framebuffer top/bottom edges over
adjacent lines. Bumping vtotal so the extra lines land in blanking
fixes the garbled strips at the panel edges (originally with 20,
the panels are idiosyncratic here).
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
index b82a5efc4..6b0507a9c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-simple.c
@@ -1906,7 +1906,7 @@ static const struct drm_display_mode eink_ed103tc2_mode[] ={
 		.vdisplay = 1404,
 		.vsync_start = 1404 + 12,
 		.vsync_end = 1404 + 12 + 1,
-		.vtotal = 1404 + 12 + 1 + 4,
+		.vtotal = 1404 + 12 + 1 + 11,
 		.flags = DRM_MODE_FLAG_PHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC |
 			 DRM_MODE_FLAG_HSKEW | DRM_MODE_FLAG_CLKDIV2,
